---
source: tests/stages.rs
expression: reports.report(path)
input_file: tests/fixtures/expand/doc_kernel_type_pages.knv
---
(def i64-page "i64\n\nHolds a signed 64-bit integer, as Rust's `i64` does.\n\nAn integer literal whose type stays open defaults to `i64`.\n\n(the i64 3)\n=> 3\n\n(infer 1)\n=> \"i64\"")
(def true-page "true\n\nIs the [bool] value true.\n\nIt is a kernel constant, so macro code and program code see the same\nbooleans.\n\n(if true 1 2)\n=> 1")
(def where-page "(where (variable (variable trait ...) ...) type)\n\nBinds the type variables of a type and the traits each must implement.\n\nA bare variable takes any type, and `(variable trait ...)` requires each\ntrait, so `(where ((n number)) (fn (n) n))` emits `fn<N: Number>(N) -> N`.\n\n(infer unwrap)\n=> \"(where (a) (fn ((option a)) a))\"")
(def hole-page "_\n\nStands for a type that inference fills in.\n\nIn a [match] pattern, `_` matches any value, and `(new _ base ...)` updates\na struct whose type comes from its base.\n\n(the (vec _) (vec 1))\n=> (vec 1)\n\n(match 3 (_ \"any\"))\n=> \"any\"")
